  "reading": "Compare mean_absolute_movement across arms before reading any quadrant gap: the objective difference is first of all a difference in how far the transition moved the model. For discrimination use the log odds ratio, not the risk ratio -- where a benign rate rests on a few prompts the risk ratio is unstable and its interval says so, while the Haldane-corrected log odds ratio stays finite at a rate of exactly 0 or 1."
}
